  "totalDurationMs": 51117,
  "firstAssistantEventMs": 51117,
  "actionResultText": "Here's your interactive Spark! 🎉 Here's how to use it:\n\n---\n\n### 🟥 Drag Point P\nClick and drag the **red point P** left or right along the curve $f(x) = x^2$. Watch all the slopes update in real time.\n\n---\n\n### 🟡 Shrink Δx with the Slider\nThe **Δx slider** controls how far the blue point Q is from P.\n\n- **Large Δx** → the dashed yellow **secant line** cuts broadly across the curve\n- **Shrink Δx → 0** → the secant line **rotates and locks onto** the green **tangent line**\n\n---\n\n### 💡 The Core Idea\n\nThe derivative is defined as exactly this limit:\n\n$$f'(x) = \\lim_{\\Delta x \\to 0} \\frac{f(x + \\Delta x) - f(x)}{\\Delta x}$$\n\n| Line | Slope formula | Color |\n|------|--------------|-------|\n| Secant (approx) | $\\dfrac{f(x+\\Delta x)-f(x)}{\\Delta x}$ | 🟡 Yellow dashed |\n| Tangent (exact) | $f'(x) = 2x$ | 🟢 Green solid |\n\nWatch the **Δslope** box in the bottom right — it measures the error between the two. As you slide Δx toward zero, the error vanishes. That *vanishing difference* **is** the derivative.",
